From f744c11e6ee452d7cdc2786a9b9290b62c8fc5be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 11:34:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] rdna-boosts: block 15: campaign memory wins

The RDNA memory campaign, squashed into one block: six validated wins that
remove ~3.4 GiB/GPU of compute-buffer VRAM and ~1.2 GiB of host buffer on
qwen4exp (ctx 204800 / ub 2048 / q8_0 KV), plus ~800 MiB/GPU + 800 MiB host
on every dense model, at a measured ~1.3 % prefill / ~0.3 % decode cost.
Each win keeps an environment kill-switch for A/B (the V4 arm is opt-in).

W1 - QSA score-chain memory (GGML_QSA_SCORE_MEM, default 1)
  relu before the 4-D reshape (elementwise, bit-identical, but it stops the
  allocator from holding the mul_mat result and its relu simultaneously) +
  n_blocks-chunked assembly with ggml_concat past a size threshold.
  qwen4exp ub 2048: 6690.40 -> 4450.40 MiB/GPU.

W2 - derived QSA per-block bias + derived visibility (GGML_QSA_DERIVED_BIAS,
  GGML_QSA_DERIVED_VIS, LLAMA_QSA_SPARSE_FA, defaults 1/1/sparse): the
  n_blocks x n_tps F32 bias tensor and the additive kq mask are no longer
  materialised; the fused top-k/FA kernels derive both in-kernel from
  compact per-cell state.  Includes the input-fill null guards (a tensor the
  graph never consumes is left unallocated by the gallocr, so every
  fill site must tolerate buffer == nullptr) and the llm_graph_input_attn_k
  null-mask guard.  qwen4exp ub 2048: 4450.40 -> 3251.39 MiB/GPU, host
  1262.70 -> 63.69 MiB.

W3 - keys-only QSA indexer cache (LLAMA_QSA_KEYS_ONLY, default 1): the
  indexer scores blocks of keys and never reads a stored value, so its
  cache is created with no V tensor.  Indexer KV 956.26 -> 318.76 MiB/GPU
  at ctx 204800 (the store is replicated on every GPU).

W4 - ggml-alloc: release view sources whose views are never consumed (the
  counting pass increments view_src->n_views for every view node, but the
  free pass only decrements it when the view is released - a view with no
  consumers is never released, so the inflated count blocks the view
  source's release and in-place reuse).  Repro 56.00 -> 16.00 MiB.  No gate:
  it is a bug fix, A/B with beta/block-15-campaign-wins/ab/w4-revert.patch.

V3 - derived kq mask for the plain attention path (LLAMA_KQ_MASK_DERIVED,
  default 1): the packed n_kv x n_tps F16 mask and its host mirror are no
  longer materialised - the MMA FA kernel derives each cell's visibility
  from compact per-cell state (GGML_OP_FLASH_ATTN_EXT gains src[5..7]: cell
  positions, per-token hi/lo bounds).  The packed tensor is still created in
  every graph, so it simply ends up with no consumer: the allocator leaves
  it unallocated and the existing fill guards skip the fill (no model list,
  no consumer can be mis-served).  The predicate is proven cell-by-cell
  value-identical (including both SWA cache variants and non-causal) and
  gates itself off on every unsupported case (alibi, multi-sequence,
  small/verify batches, non-MMA backends, M-RoPE ext clause).  Dense models:
  -799.20 MiB/GPU and -799.21 MiB host; gemma-4-E4B (ISWA) -809.18/-809.18;
  gemma-4-31B (ISWA) -811.17/-811.18; scaling exactly n_kv x n_tps x 2 B.
  The backend support probe is skipped entirely on a multi-stream KV cache
  (n_seq_max > 1 without kv_unified, and deepseek4, which keeps per-sequence
  streams even in unified mode): it forces a single-sequence probe graph, and
  on such a cache deepseek4's indexer stream layout asserts, while the derived
  form is unreachable there anyway (kq_mask_derivable() requires a single
  stream).

V4 - native q8_0 K/V in the flash-attention kernels (GGML_CUDA_FA_KV_NATIVE,
  OPT-IN, default 0): the whole-cache F16 staging scratch and its per-ubatch
  conversion are replaced by dequantising each 16-byte staged chunk while
  the shared K/V tiles are loaded (a chunk is 8 elements = a quarter q8_0
  block, and every MMA/TILE batch is a multiple of 8 elements, so a chunk
  never straddles a block).  The staged values are bit-identical to
  dequantize_block_q8_0_f16.  Dense models: -744 MiB/GPU (4B), -632 (27B),
  -1224 (gemma-4-31B) at ctx 204800/ub 2048, more at smaller ub; qwen4exp
  unchanged.  Ships opt-in: it costs ~1.7-1.9 % prefill (the lost cp_async
  pipeline - a quantized source cannot be copied asynchronously) with a
  large memory win and no cheap way to close the gap; decode is untouched.
  TILE and VEC already read bf16/f16 natively.

Validation (2026-09-10, 3x R9700/RDNA4, ctx 204800, q8_0 KV unless noted;
full record: beta/block-15-campaign-wins/):
- reserve matrix, all five models x ub 2048/1024/512 x V4 off/on: every
  number matches the per-win records (the wins compose additively:
  -2240 W1, -1199 W2, 0/-637.5 W3, -799 V3, -744/-632 V4 per GPU).
- same-seed generated text byte-identical on 4B, 27B, gemma-4-E4B (ISWA),
  gemma-4-31B (ISWA) and qwen4exp across every gate combination (V3 on/off
  x V4 on/off; qwen4exp W1/W2/W3/W4/V3/V4 flips - 7 configurations), at a
  short and a 40k-token prompt.
- adaptive-MTP gate unchanged: 27B inline draft 0.76744 (66/86, mean 3.28)
  identical in all four gate combinations; qwen4exp draft 0.44262 (54/122)
  identical in all six, and equal to the block-14 baseline; MTP still
  +26 % over plain decode.
- test-backend-ops: FLASH_ATTN_EXT on ROCm0 (both V4 gates) and CPU, the
  derived FA cases, VIEW/CONT/CPY/DUP/CONCAT; test-alloc and
  test-batch-alloc; the W4 repro goes 56.00 -> 16.00 MiB and the revert
  patch restores ggml-alloc.c byte-identically.
- prefill cost, interleaved same-binary A/B: V3 -1.28 % pp20480/ub 2048 on
  the 4B (the 27B is neutral, +0.28 %), V4 a further -1.85 % (4B) /
  -1.72 % (27B); decode within noise in every case.

Known pre-existing issue found during this validation (NOT introduced here,
reproduces on block 14): gemma-4-E4B-it on 3 GPUs with -sm tensor aborts in
the meta splitter (ggml-backend-meta.cpp:1177, a FLASH_ATTN_EXT node whose K
source has zero extent on one buffer because n_head_kv = 2 < 3 devices).
It works on 1 GPU, on 2 GPUs, and on 3 GPUs with -sm layer.  All other
models are unaffected.  Out of scope for this block.

Beta staging, gate table and the full validation record:
beta/block-15-campaign-wins/README.md; the per-win designs:
wip/arch-independent-memory/{V3-DERIVED-KQ-MASK-PLAN,V4-NATIVE-Q8-KV-PLAN,
DERIVED-MASK-DESIGN}.md and wip/qwen4exp/qsa-memory/.

Amended 2026-09-10 with V5 - native bf16 K/V in the MMA flash-attention
kernel (gated by the SAME GGML_CUDA_FA_KV_NATIVE switch as V4, default 0,
i.e. opt-in): a bf16 K/V cache no longer needs the F16 staging scratch.  A
bf16 source row and the F16 tile it feeds have the same byte layout (2
bytes per element, 16-byte chunks), so the MMA loader converts each staged
chunk in registers (bf16 -> f32 -> f16, bit-identical to the launcher's
ggml_get_to_fp16_cuda(GGML_TYPE_BF16)) instead of copying it, and the
scratch sizing plus the whole-cache conversion pass are skipped for that
operand.  The staging source is now a single type code
(fattn_kv_native_t{FATTN_KV_NATIVE_NONE,Q8_0,BF16}) shared by the launcher,
the alloc-size query and both kernels, so they cannot disagree on whether
the scratch exists (the old use_q8_K/use_q8_V flags are subsumed).

- reserve (ctx 204800, ub 2048, bf16 KV, arm on): 4B 968.86 -> 256.86,
  27B 1072.86 -> 488.86, gemma-4-E4B (ISWA) 1062.89 -> 404.89,
  gemma-4-31B (ISWA) 2068.89 -> 716.89 MiB/GPU - exactly the F16 cache's
  footprint; ub 1024/512 win 756/778 (4B) and 746 (27B); qwen4exp is
  unaffected (its FA path never staged bf16 - f16 == bf16 == on/off there),
  and the TILE/VEC paths already read bf16 natively (ub 8: 8.09 both ways).
- same-seed generated text byte-identical (bf16 native vs staged vs f16) on
  4B, 27B, gemma-4-E4B and gemma-4-31B, short and 3k/40k-token prompts,
  with the V3 derived mask active; the two wins are additive (4B: derived
  mask -799.2 MiB, bf16 scratch -712.0 MiB, both verified independently).
- adaptive-MTP gate unchanged: 27B 0.82716 and qwen4exp 0.44262 identical
  with the arm on and off; the recorded q8_0 references (27B 0.76744,
  qwen4exp 0.44262) are unchanged by the refactor.
- test-backend-ops FLASH_ATTN_EXT: 7859/7859 on ROCm0 and CPU; the 2704
  bf16 K/V cases (every head size, including the 576/512 MLA V-is-K-view
  layout) and the 365 q8_0 cases pass with the arm on and off, with
  identical case lists.
- prefill cost (interleaved same-binary A/B, arm off -> on): the conversion
  itself is free (native bf16 staging measures within 0.2 % of an F16
  cache), but dropping the scratch costs 4B -0.2 % (pp2048), +0.3 % (8192),
  -1.06 % (20480), -2.36 % (40960) and 27B -0.76 % (20480); decode is
  within 0.1 % everywhere.  The launcher's F16 copy is a dense, normalized
  copy of the cache view (the GQA heads are interleaved - for the 4B nb[1]
  is 2048 B for a 512 B row), and the native path re-reads that view on
  every staging pass.  Hence opt-in, exactly like V4 (D9: a sub-2 % loss
  with a large memory win and no cheap fix ships behind a switch).

Mixed K/V cache types (bf16+q8_0, f16+q8_0, either direction) remain a
pre-existing trap, documented but not fixed here: the attention falls off
the GPU kernel path (graph splits 18 vs 2, ~1.5 GiB host compute buffer,
4B pp2048 7924 -> 640-1049 t/s).  Same-type K/V is the practical choice.

2026-09-10 RDNA3_5 (gfx1151) amendment: V3 (derived kq mask) now
engages on a ROCm/HIP iGPU.  The probe rejected
GGML_BACKEND_DEVICE_TYPE_IGPU as "not the CUDA/HIP backend", so on
Strix Halo V3 was silently disabled and its ~800 MiB compute + ~800 MiB
host win was lost.  The device-type gate now accepts IGPU (the ROCm/HIP
reg name is still required), and the derived form additionally requires
a single KV stream: build_attn_mha derives the attention stream count
from the KV tensor (k->ne[3] == the cache's n_stream), so with
n_seq_max > 1 -- even for a single-sequence ubatch -- the derived tok_lo
was built for one stream while Q was reshaped for n_seq_max streams and
the shape assert in ggml_flash_attn_ext_add_kq_derived aborted context
creation.  kq_mask_derivable() now rejects n_stream != 1, so a
multi-slot context keeps the packed mask (no crash) and a single-stream
context gets the win.

Validated on Strix Halo (gfx1151, ROCm 7.14): V3 on/off byte-identical
over 7 KV/arm configs x 16 runs x 129 tokens (2064 gate cells each);
reserves reproduce the RDNA4 numbers exactly (4B ctx 204800/ub 2048:
V3 -799.20 MiB compute / -799.21 host, V5 bf16 968.86 -> 256.86, V4 q8_0
1001.13 -> 257.13); the derived test-backend-ops cases pass on ROCm0;
and llama-server --parallel 4 (the config that aborted before) now
serves and passes the 16-run gate.  Discrete GPUs are unaffected (they
report GGML_BACKEND_DEVICE_TYPE_GPU and normally have n_stream == 1).

Amended 2026-09-11 (9th re-cut): fix a variable-shadowing bug in build_attn_qsa that broke the
LLAMA_QSA_SPARSE_FA=0 dense arm for every model/type.  The V2/V3 refactor wrapped the top-k mask
chain in `if (kq_mask != nullptr) { ... }` and added an outer `kq_mask_top_k` declaration, leaving
the chain's own `ggml_tensor * kq_mask_top_k = ggml_set_rows(...)` inside the block as a NEW local.
The chain was therefore built (whenever the mask existed) but its result never reached the
attention: build_attn_mha got the outer `nullptr`, the chain's nodes were unreachable from the
graph output (so ggml never emitted them), the packed mask lost its only consumer (so the
allocator dropped it and set_input_kq_mask was skipped), and the dense arm attended with no mask
at all - a full causal leak.  Observed as qwen4exp perplexity ~1.02-1.06 on every KV type
(delivery: 6.49-6.55), and as ~1.03 on RANDOM text (delivery ~18.4), with dense-arm greedy text
differing from the delivery.  Fixed by assigning the block's result to the outer variable
(dropping the inner `ggml_tensor *`).  The production (sparse) arm never enters that block, so it
is bit-identical before and after.  See beta/block-15-campaign-wins/BETA-TESTING.md 4c and
WORKLOG.md 2026-09-11 (11).

2026-09-14 amendment (issue #30, "wider configuration"): V4 is no longer opt-in for
the sub-F16 quantized cache types, and q4_0 gains a native arm.

  - GGML_CUDA_FA_KV_NATIVE is now a three-state policy: unset = auto (native
    q8_0/q4_0 ON, native bf16 OFF), =1 forces both on, =0 forces the pre-amendment
    F16-staging path (the escape hatch).  The whole-cache F16 staging pass is
    proportional to n_kv and runs on every decode step, so removing it for the
    sub-F16 quants is worth +23 % tg64 at d65536 on gfx1201 (q8_0 18.92 -> 23.29
    vs stock 22.43) at ~1.2 % prefill, and it recovers ~744 MiB/GPU of scratch.
  - Native q4_0 arm beside q8_0/bf16 (ggml_cuda_fattn_dequantize_q4_0_chunk,
    arithmetic-identical to convert.cu's dequantize_block_q4_0) in the tile and
    MMA kernels: q4_0 d65536 19.72 -> 22.82 vs stock 21.03, ~1.3 % prefill.
  - Bit-identical to the staging path (same-seed greedy text) and width-pure
    (W = 1..8 one logits hash per KV type); MTP n_max 3 acceptance unchanged
    (0.75182).  Full evidence: wip/issue-30-mtp-decode-regression/MEASUREMENTS.md.
  - Side effect: also fixes the adaptive-MTP high-context load failure
    (--spec-draft-n-max 12 -c 196608 q8_0, default 4 slots): the F16 staging
    scratch was exactly the 260 MiB the draft context was short, so it now loads
    and generates.

2026-09-15 amendment (issue #30, the reporter's r3 review): the q4_0 NaN fix, the prefill band
split, and native arms for the last four quantized K/V types.

  - Mixed-K/V kernel contract (the reporter's 4 NaN failures in test-backend-ops -o
    FLASH_ATTN_EXT).  The tile kernel is instantiated with ONE type_KV for both operands and
    builds its native descriptors from that compile-time type, while launch_fattn chose its
    native read per tensor; a mixed pair (K=q4_0, V=f16) therefore fell back to the F16 tile
    with K's staging skipped, and the kernel read raw q4_0 as F16.  launch_fattn now takes the
    kernel's native type explicitly (kv_native_kernel; the tile passes its type_KV, the vec
    passes NONE, the MMA keeps per-operand semantics).  llama.cpp rejects mixed caches, so only
    the op test could see it.
  - ggml_cuda_flash_attn_ext_get_alloc_size's TILE case never learned the q4_0 arm, so a q4_0
    cache kept reserving the F16 scratch the launcher no longer used: -c 196608 q4_0
    849.04 -> 123.04 MiB -- the arm's memory win had never actually been delivered.
  - Prefill band split: a prefill (n_q > 8) stages the operand into F16 while decode/verify
    (n_q <= 8) keeps the native read, recovering the quantized-KV prefill cost (q8_0 pp150000
    661.0 -> 691.4 on 1 GPU, 996.0 -> 1076.9 on 2, 1111.4 -> 1199.0 on 3; q4_0 694.5).  The
    staging scratch comes from a new per-context, per-stream arena
    (ggml_backend_cuda_context::fattn_stage / fattn_stage_get) instead of the compute-graph
    reserve, which sized it for n_ctx (~726 MiB at a 200k context) even though the real
    scratch tracks the prefix; a multi-token graph is never CUDA-graph captured, so a runtime
    allocation there is safe.  Bounded by GGML_CUDA_FA_STAGE_MAX_MB (default 512 MiB, 0 =
    unbounded).  Arch-gated: RDNA3_5 keeps the native read at prefill (it wins at every depth
    there: gfx1151 9B q8_0 pp16k 1410 vs 1405, pp65k 1059 vs 1043), RDNA4/RDNA3_0 stage.
  - Native arms for q4_1 / q5_0 / q5_1 / iq4_nl (ggml_cuda_fattn_dequantize_{q4_1,q5_0,q5_1,
    iq4_nl}_chunk, arithmetic-identical to convert.cu), closing the last gap in the V4 set --
    the four types stage through F16 otherwise.  tg64 @ d32768 staged -> native: gfx1201
    +9.9/+10.8/+12.5/+8.8 % (q4_1 23.14 -> 25.44, q5_0 22.16 -> 24.56, q5_1 22.23 -> 25.00,
    iq4_nl 22.92 -> 24.94) with prefill unchanged; gfx1151 (9B) +22.9/+26.0/+26.7/+22.0 % for a
    0.6-1.1 % prefill cost.  Two bugs the op test caught on the way: the tile loader chose the
    native branch with a hand-written `type_KV == Q8_0 || Q4_0` test (the new instantiations
    then took the F16 branch and read an unwritten staging buffer -- the hsk=72 NaNs), and the
    q5_0/q5_1 chunk helpers took the low nibble in both halves.
  - Same-seed greedy text is bit-identical native vs staging for all eight KV types on both
    arches, and test-backend-ops -o FLASH_ATTN_EXT is 5951/5951 on both.  Width purity: gfx1151
    pure for all eight types; gfx1201 pure except the documented pre-existing q4_0 logits-level
    band edges (GREEDY-PURITY.md 36, whose guarantee is now stated at the text/acceptance
    level).

2026-09-15 amendment (build time): the tile kernel's native-KV type axis is instantiated in the
generated template-instance TUs again instead of implicitly in the tile dispatch TU.

Block 03 turned type_KV into a template parameter of ggml_cuda_flash_attn_ext_tile_case so the tile
kernel could read BF16 (and later the quantized types) natively, while DECL_FATTN_TILE_CASE /
EXTERN_DECL_FATTN_TILE_CASES kept covering only F16/BF16.  Because the dispatch in fattn-tile.cu has an
unconditional `case` per native type, the other six types were then instantiated *implicitly in that
TU*: 12 head-size combinations x 6 types = 72 case instantiations (96 symbols including the 24 externed
F16/BF16), each pulling in both softcap variants and the whole ncols2 chain.  With block 08's
FA_QUANTS default (8 diagonal pairs) that single TU took 509 s of a 538 s `-j16` backend build on a
16-core machine (measured 2026-09-15, gfx1201) -- it *was* the critical path, and no amount of build
parallelism could help.

The macros now cover every type the dispatch can select, so the 12 generated
template-instances/fattn-tile-instance-*.cu files instantiate 8 cases each and the dispatch TU holds
only `extern` declarations.  Build time: `ggml-hip` 538 s -> 330 s, and the tile dispatch TU itself
drops from 509 s to under 10 s.

The remaining critical path is the `fattn-mma-f16` instance set, and that one is ours too: this
block's native-KV arms instantiate the whole WMMA kernel once per KV type *inside every instance TU*
(the arm chain in `ggml_cuda_flash_attn_ext_mma_f16_case`), so each of the 21 instance files compiles
8 kernel copies.  Measured on the same TU (`ncols1_4-ncols2_4`): object 0.90 MB -> 7.26 MB, compile
6.7 s -> 229 s.  Fixing it needs either a finer generated-file granularity (~21 -> ~150 TUs) or a
runtime KV-type dispatch in the WMMA loader, i.e. a code-path change with its own A/B, so it is left
as a follow-up rather than folded in here.
Nothing about the kernels changed -- same template arguments, same flags, same device code; only the TU
that emits them differs.  Verified: `test-backend-ops -o FLASH_ATTN_EXT` 5951/5951 with zero failures,
the 27B prose text hashes bit-identical to the pre-amendment build (q8_0 472b282950b5, q4_0
118eb7f5fe85, f16 70960317a203), and `tg64@32768`/`pp8192` reproduce the recorded values within
run-to-run noise across five KV types.

Amended 2026-09-17: the HIP build now passes `-Wno-pass-failed`.  The FA
kernels carry bare `#pragma unroll` hints on runtime-bounded loops, so AMDGPU
clang reports every one it cannot honour; the native-KV arms instantiate the
WMMA kernel per KV type per instance TU and multiply that into ~10k "loop not
unrolled" warning lines per clean build.  The hints are advisory and the pass
already failed, so the build output is unchanged -- only the flood is gone.
HIP-only (the diagnostic is Clang/AMDGPU).  See wip/build-time-regression/.

Amended 2026-09-18: the tile template instances are generated per (head size, KV type) instead of
per head size, matching the per-type axis this block introduced.  Build-time only: the same 96
instantiations, identical symbols.

Amended 2026-09-25 (issue #45): the RDNA4 GQA-6 decode/verify flash-attention band.

At head 256 with GQA 6, the tile kernel can only fold ncols2 = 2 (its ncols2 must divide
the GQA ratio), so the whole n_q <= 8 band fetched and dequantized every K/V element once
per head pair -- three times per query row at 276 GB/s on q8_0.  The band now routes the
whole band (n_q = 1 included) to the WMMA kernel with the GQA group folded into ncols2 = 8
(existing (256, ncols1 4|2, ncols2 8) instances, no new instantiations): one block covers
the group, and the KV is split round-robin over a fixed P = nsm blocks per output tile
(launch_fattn, GGML_HIP_FA_BAND_WMMA_SPLIT override).  P depends on neither n_q nor the KV
length, so decode and every verify width accumulate the same partials in the same order --
the round-robin form is what keeps the GREEDY-PURITY band invariant (a contiguous stream-k
split moved its split points with the 256-padded KV length and broke it).

- kernel chooser, ncols dispatcher and launch_fattn share one self-contained predicate
  (ggml_cuda_fattn_band_wmma_applies), and launch_fattn also requires the ncols2 == 8
  template parameter, so a disagreement can never launch the 2-D grid into a kernel whose
  fast path is compiled out.
- coverage follows ggml_cuda_fattn_kv_native_type, not a hand-written type list: every
  native quantized K/V type wins (q8_0, q4_0, q4_1, q5_0, q5_1, iq4_nl); f16 stays on tile
  (DRAM-bound) and bf16 stays on tile while its native arm is opt-in.
- default ON (maintainer policy); GGML_HIP_FA_BAND_WMMA=0 opts out (=2 picks ncols1 = 2).
  GGML_CUDA_FA_WMMA_256=0 / GGML_CUDA_FA_WMMA_MAX_HEAD<256 still disable the band.

Measured on gfx1201 (R9700), 27B qwen35 head 256 GQA 6, q8_0 KV, op level kv 16384
(tile -> band, us/run): n_q 3 326 -> 150, n_q 5 524 -> 225, n_q 8 814 -> 230; n_q 1
141 -> 148 (q4_0/q4_1/iq4_nl are faster at n_q 1 too).  End to end, 27B UD-Q4_K_XL
draft-mtp n3 at ~40k ctx, band off -> on: 1 GPU 43.3 -> 51.3, 2 GPU tensor 67.9 -> 76.6,
3 GPU tensor 77.6 -> 88.8 t/s (+13-18 %), while pp512/2048/4096 are flat (the band is
gated to n_q <= 8, so prefill is untouched by construction).

Purity re-verified with the band on: test-backend-ops -o FLASH_ATTN_EXT 6340/6340 on
ROCm0 (389 GQA-6 cases across all eight KV types, both layouts); plain == draft-mtp
byte-identical on all eight KV types at ~40k ctx, 3-GPU tensor (acceptance 0.83-0.86),
and q8_0/q4_0 text identical across --spec-draft-n-max 3/5/7 (verify widths 4/6/8);
1 GPU layer, 2/3 GPU tensor and 3 GPU layer are all pure.  New qwen35-band eval and
perf cases added to tests/test-backend-ops.cpp.
